        "comments": "The assembly csSphSqua2.1 is based on 291x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, the primary assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 21 (450 ? 1,681 Kbp) are unknown. Chromosomes 21 and 22 show substantially higher coverage than the other chromosomes. This is consistent with the karyotype reported by Yu et al. (2023, Nature Plants), which describes 19 autosomes plus 2 small sex chromosomes in this species, suggesting chromosomes 21 and 22 may correspond to the sex chromosomes.",
